{"id": "spec-1-english", "tags": ["spec"], "input": "Hi, I want to order 20 kg of Jasmine rice to be delivered to Jalan Ampang this Friday.", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "Jasmine rice", "quantity": 20, "unit": "kg", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": "Jalan Ampang", "delivery_date": "this Friday"}, "note": "INTENDED DIVERGENCE: the spec's expected output is \"Friday\", but our rule is verbatim dates and the message says \"this Friday\". The spec is inconsistent here - it keeps the determiner in \"下星期一\" (next Monday) and returns \"tomorrow\" unchanged. Decision recorded in STATUS.md.", "spec_expected_delivery_date": "Friday"}
{"id": "spec-2-mandarin", "tags": ["spec"], "input": "我要订购5箱苹果，下星期一送去吉隆坡。", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "苹果", "quantity": 5, "unit": "箱", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": "吉隆坡", "delivery_date": "下星期一"}}
