{"id": "spec-4-missing-details", "tags": ["spec"], "input": "Can I get 3 cartons of Coke (1kg)?", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "Coke", "quantity": 3, "unit": "cartons", "packing_size": "1kg"}], "delivery_location": null, "delivery_date": null}}
{"id": "spec-5-multiple-items", "tags": ["spec"], "input": "I want to order 2 kg of Jasmine rice (10kg pack) and 5 boxes of eggs.", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "Jasmine rice", "quantity": 2, "unit": "kg", "packing_size": "10kg pack"}, {"product_name": "eggs", "quantity": 5, "unit": "boxes", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": null, "delivery_date": null}}
{"id": "spec-6-list-form", "tags": ["spec"], "input": "Fish fillet-5ctn\nPrawn meat -1ctn\nKing prawn-\nCwp bill on next month", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "Fish fillet", "quantity": 5, "unit": "ctn", "packing_size": null}, {"product_name": "Prawn meat", "quantity": 1, "unit": "ctn", "packing_size": null}, {"product_name": "King prawn", "quantity": 0, "unit": null, "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": null, "delivery_date": null}, "note": "The hardest spec case: a non-order line must be dropped entirely, and a missing quantity becomes 0 rather than null."}
{"id": "spec-7-packing-size", "tags": ["spec"], "input": "Boneless chicken 10kg\nPork chop bone in 5kg\nBeef brisket 5kg\nBeef short plate 1mm 2kg\n\nDeliver 1 Oct", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "Boneless chicken", "quantity": 10, "unit": "kg", "packing_size": null}, {"product_name": "Pork chop bone in", "quantity": 5, "unit": "kg", "packing_size": null}, {"product_name": "Beef brisket", "quantity": 5, "unit": "kg", "packing_size": null}, {"product_name": "Beef short plate", "quantity": 2, "unit": "kg", "packing_size": "1mm"}], "delivery_location": null, "delivery_date": "1 Oct"}, "note": "Tests the quantity-vs-packing_size rule: one measurement is the quantity, two means the descriptor is the packing size."}
{"id": "reg-1-verb-code-switch", "tags": ["regression", "mixed"], "input": "我要order 5 boxes of eggs, send to Penang 明天", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "eggs", "quantity": 5, "unit": "boxes", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": "Penang", "delivery_date": "明天"}}
{"id": "reg-2-chinese-unit-english-product", "tags": ["regression", "mixed"], "input": "Pls send 10箱 Milo 2kg pack to 吉隆坡 tomorrow", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "Milo", "quantity": 10, "unit": "箱", "packing_size": "2kg"}], "delivery_location": "吉隆坡", "delivery_date": "tomorrow"}, "note": "Each field keeps its own language: English product, Chinese unit, in one item. KNOWN AMBIGUITY: the model sometimes returns \"2kg pack\" here. The brief supports both - example 3 drops the word pack, example 5 keeps it - so no prompt rule can satisfy both."}
{"id": "reg-3-mixed-list-form", "tags": ["regression", "mixed"], "input": "Boneless chicken 10kg\n苹果 5箱\nPrawn meat-2ctn\n送去槟城 1 Oct", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "Boneless chicken", "quantity": 10, "unit": "kg", "packing_size": null}, {"product_name": "苹果", "quantity": 5, "unit": "箱", "packing_size": null}, {"product_name": "Prawn meat", "quantity": 2, "unit": "ctn", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": "槟城", "delivery_date": "1 Oct"}}
{"id": "reg-4-chinese-products-english-frame", "tags": ["regression", "mixed"], "input": "I want 3 cartons of 可乐 and 2kg 鸡胸肉 delivered this Friday", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "可乐", "quantity": 3, "unit": "cartons", "packing_size": null}, {"product_name": "鸡胸肉", "quantity": 2, "unit": "kg", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": null, "delivery_date": "this Friday"}}
{"id": "reg-5-romanised-malay", "tags": ["regression", "mixed"], "input": "Tolong hantar 5 ctn Milo ke Johor esok, 谢谢", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "Milo", "quantity": 5, "unit": "ctn", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": "Johor", "delivery_date": "esok"}, "note": "Malay, which we never designed for. Works because nothing in the pipeline branches on language."}
{"id": "reg-6-chinese-numeral", "tags": ["regression"], "input": "我要三箱苹果，送到槟城", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "苹果", "quantity": 3, "unit": "箱", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": "槟城", "delivery_date": null}}
{"id": "reg-7-chinese-numeral-over-ten", "tags": ["regression"], "input": "订二十公斤茉莉香米，下星期五", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "茉莉香米", "quantity": 20, "unit": "公斤", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": null, "delivery_date": "下星期五"}}
{"id": "reg-8-fractional-quantity", "tags": ["regression"], "input": "Half kg beef and 1.5kg chicken to Ipoh", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "beef", "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "kg", "packing_size": null}, {"product_name": "chicken", "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "kg", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": "Ipoh", "delivery_date": null}, "note": "Why quantity is a float and not an int: an int field would truncate 0.5 to 0, which postprocess would then flag as 'quantity missing'."}
{"id": "reg-9-same-product-two-languages", "tags": ["regression", "mixed"], "input": "苹果 3箱\napple 2 boxes", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "苹果", "quantity": 3, "unit": "箱", "packing_size": null}, {"product_name": "apple", "quantity": 2, "unit": "boxes", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": null, "delivery_date": null}, "note": "Two items for one real-world product. Correct for this scope - product matching is out of scope - but a downstream catalogue matcher would need to reconcile them."}
{"id": "reg-10-traditional-characters", "tags": ["regression"], "input": "我要訂購5箱蘋果，下星期一送去吉隆坡", "expected": {"items": [{"product_name": "蘋果", "quantity": 5, "unit": "箱", "packing_size": null}], "delivery_location": "吉隆坡", "delivery_date": "下星期一"}, "note": "NFKC deliberately does not fold traditional to simplified, so the customer's own script survives."}
